# Product Decisions

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M0 Confirm the brief and public business facts
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Separate the user's requirements, proposed defaults and verified business facts.

## Tasks

- [x] Record a vegetarian home bakery, real cake photography and personal ordering.
- [x] Record planning/assets first, before website implementation.
- [x] Accept the five supplied screenshots as prototype inputs, not a full archive.
- [x] Record restrained image edits: preserve the actual cake and original files.
- [x] Record future handoff by extracted export folder path alone.
- [x] Record October 4 authorization to implement without questions until a prototype is ready.
- [x] Use the supplied profile as the working brand/Instagram contact, with unknown
  WhatsApp, prices and service facts omitted instead of invented.
- [x] Implement the earlier three-section reduction with readable text/direct links;
  record its later supersession by the story restoration in workstream 09.
- [x] Record the user's choice of separate background-removed cakes with white contours.
- [x] Restore only the original story/note directly under the hero; keep FAQs,
  forms and a separate custom-cake section out.
- [x] User chose Whisk & Crumbs and approved updating the name, logo and favicon;
  use Home-baked vegetarian cakes as the descriptor. Legal availability is unverified.
- [ ] Confirm products, descriptions, sizes, portions, prices and seasonal availability.
- [ ] Confirm vegetarian/eggless wording, allergens and made-to-order preparation.
- [ ] Confirm lead time, city/service area, pickup/delivery rules and fees.
- [ ] Confirm a public contact number, contact hours and optional email.
- [ ] Agree on availability confirmation, payment methods and cancellation policy.
- [ ] Approve WhatsApp as primary and Instagram as secondary contact.
- [ ] Confirm whether a public phone/email fallback is wanted; forms are out of scope.
- [ ] Approve which contact details may be public; do not expose a home address by default.
- [x] Keep new biography, portraits and reviews outside the approved restored-story scope.
- [ ] Resolve hosting: GitHub for source, an appropriate static host for orders.
- [x] Obtain authorization for prototype implementation.
- [ ] Obtain approval of the resulting design and final launch-ready scope.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Public claims and product data come from the baker, not guesses from a photo.
- [ ] Eggless is not presented as vegan or allergen-free.
- [ ] An enquiry is not called a confirmed order; manual confirmation is explicit.
- [ ] Hosting and public contact choices have actual user approval.

## Completion evidence

- Supplied 19-page specification: ..\docs\references\home-bakery-design-specification.pdf.
- Proposed options and verified hosting constraint: ..\docs\website-plan.md.
- 2026-10-04 user messages authorize prototype screenshots and minimal edits;
  later explicitly authorize implementation without further questions. No prices,
  service terms, public phone number or final visual acceptance were supplied.
- Later explicit user request: "I liked the our little story part tho, lets bring
  that back right belw the first section"; chosen treatment: "Cut out each cake,
  remove its background and add a white sticker outline (Recommended)".
  These approve scope, not final visual quality or publication.

